## 📝 Code Logic & Component Breakdown

* **`extract_ips(log_path)`**: Leverages boundary-restricted Regular Expressions (`r"\b(?:\d{1,3}\.){3}\d{1,3}\b"`) to act like a precision comb, scanning chaotic line strings to isolate cleanly structured IPv4 addresses.
* **`flag_suspicious(ip_list)`**: Utilizes Python's low-overhead `collections.Counter` memory array to count address frequencies instantaneously, isolating threat profiles exceeding the defined brute-force attack threshold.
* **`check_abuseipdb(ip)`**: Automates external intelligence requests using the `requests` library. Transmits secure credential headers over TLS to retrieve modern CTI malicious reputation tracking indices.
* **`verdict(score)`**: Converts abstract, numerical backend API indicators into real-world operational security levels (`HIGH RISK`, `MEDIUM RISK`, `LOW RISK`) to drive faster security triage.

